=== a one-line nested view keeps its call on one line
context: expr
prefix: {
suffix: }
--- input
            {Some(  view! { <spacer /> }  )}
--- expected
            {Some(view! { <spacer /> })}
=== combobox.rs: a broken nested view as the only argument hugs its call
context: expr
prefix: {
suffix: }
--- input
                {anchored(
                    view! {
                        <popover_panel(theme) w={width}>
                            {rows}
                        </popover_panel>
                    })}
--- expected
                {anchored(view! {
                    <popover_panel(theme) w={width}>
                        {rows}
                    </popover_panel>
                })}
=== sidebar.rs: a broken nested view among arguments breaks the call
context: expr
prefix: {
suffix: }
--- input
                {nav_row(p, view! {
                    <div class="w-4 h-4 items-center justify-center">
                        <icon svg={icons::PET} size={15.0} color={p.accent} />
                    </div>
                }, "Your dot", Msg::Noop)}
--- expected
                {nav_row(
                    p,
                    view! {
                        <div class="w-4 h-4 items-center justify-center">
                            <icon svg={icons::PET} size={15.0} color={p.accent} />
                        </div>
                    },
                    "Your dot",
                    Msg::Noop
                )}
=== a closure body keeps no block rustfmt adds when it breaks
context: expr
prefix: on:click={
suffix: }
--- input
            on:click={move |_| show_popover(anchor, view! { <text class="text-sm">"Copied to the clipboard"</text> }, Duration::from_millis(1500))}
--- expected
            on:click={move |_| show_popover(
                anchor,
                view! { <text class="text-sm">"Copied to the clipboard"</text> },
                Duration::from_millis(1500)
            )}
